From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:21:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: Default axi_daisy to 3

axi_daisy was 0 by default since 2cb98537791e ("media: apple: avd: Let axi_daisy change at run time").

Measured on the J604 in an arm-matrix session on 1.1142 (2026-11-21T11:20Z): av110-4k60 +21.6 % better (95 % interval 19.0..23.9); hevc10-4k60 +29.6 % better (95 % interval 28.0..30.4) with axi_daisy=3 against the same boot with it 0; no guard cell got worse beyond noise.

Make 3 the default; 0 still gives the behaviour before this change.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
index d19256d46ca..53c7e681f1a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
@@ -355,10 +355,10 @@ void avd_pm_apply_axi_tunables(struct avd_dev *avd)
  * nothing, 2 = read each register once and log it (an access to the
  * bridge window), 3 = program the tables in macOS's order.
  */
-static unsigned int axi_daisy;
+static unsigned int axi_daisy = 3;
 module_param(axi_daisy, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(axi_daisy,
-		 "T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy, read at each decoder power-up: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (default 0)");
+		 "T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy, read at each decoder power-up: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (default 3)");
 
 static const struct avd_tunable avd_daisy_flow_up[] = {
 	{ 0x0000, 0x800000ff, 0x80000026 }, /* UP_CMD_CREDIT_GS_ALLOC */
-- 
2.43.0

